{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790436439757,"sessionID":"ses_f21adfe5bffenhUxDN7qtJawe5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_41d7abb017b348d0af3f73b2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the project structure in /workspace. I need to understand the full directory layout, especially:\n1. All .gd files and their locations\n2. All .tscn files and their locations\n3. The contents of res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\n4. The contents of res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\n5. The contents of res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn\n6. Any existing custom_nodes directory\n7. Any references to UnitStats, BattleUnit, Team enums\n\nReturn all file paths found and the full contents of each of the key files mentioned above.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f21ada94effeuR5QrQhVWvHA7m\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is the complete report on the project structure and file contents.\n\n---\n\n## Directory Layout\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   └── filesystem_cache10\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── imported/\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   └── uid_cache.bin\n├── data/\n│   ├── enemies/\n│   │   └── zombie.tres\n│   └── units/\n│       ├── bjorn.tres\n│       ├── unit_stats.gd\n│       └── unit_stats.gd.uid\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── battle_unit/\n│   │   ├── battle_unit.gd\n│   │   └── battle_unit.tscn\n│   └── main.tscn\n├── scripts/              (empty directory)\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. All `.gd` Files and Their Locations\n\n| File | Path |\n|---|---|\n| `unit_stats.gd` | `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd` |\n| `battle_unit.gd` | `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` |\n\nThere are only two `.gd` files in the project.\n\n---\n\n## 2. All `.tscn` Files and Their Locations\n\n| File | Path |\n|---|---|\n| `battle_unit.tscn` | `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn` |\n| `main.tscn` | `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` |\n\nThere are two `.tscn` files.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Contents of `res://data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name UnitStats\nextends Resource\n\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n\nconst MAX_ATTACK_RANGE := 5\n\n@export var team: Team\n@export_range(1, MAX_ATTACK_RANGE) var attack_range: int = 1\n```\n\nThis defines the `UnitStats` resource with a `Team` enum (`PLAYER` = 0, `ENEMY` = 1), a max attack range constant, and exported properties for `team` and `attack_range`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Contents of `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name BattleUnit\nextends Area2D\n\n@export var stats: UnitStats: set = _set_stats\n\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tif stats:\n\t\t_set_stats(stats)\n\n\nfunc _set_stats(value: UnitStats) -> void:\n\tstats = value\n\t\n\tif not stats or not is_node_ready():\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\tstats = value.duplicate()\n\tcollision_layer = stats.team + 1\n```\n\nThis defines the `BattleUnit` node (extends `Area2D`). It has an exported `stats` property of type `UnitStats` with a setter. On ready (and when stats are set while the node is ready), it duplicates the stats resource and sets `collision_layer` based on the team (PLAYER=1, ENEMY=2).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Contents of `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn`\n\n**Full path:** `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn`\n\n```gdresource\n[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd\" id=\"1_battle_unit\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/units/bjorn.tres\" id=\"2_stats\"]\n\n[sub_resource type=\"RectangleShape2D\" id=\"1_body_shape\"]\nsize = Vector2(24, 24)\n\n[node name=\"BattleUnit\" type=\"Area2D\"]\ncollision_mask = 0\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")\nstats = ExtResource(\"2_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"CollisionShape2D\" type=\"CollisionShape2D\" parent=\".\"]\nshape = SubResource(\"1_body_shape\")\n```\n\nThe scene has a root `BattleUnit` node (Area2D) with a `CollisionShape2D` child using a 24x24 rectangle shape. Stats are pre-assigned to `bjorn.tres`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Custom Nodes Directory\n\nThere is **no `custom_nodes` directory** anywhere under `/workspace`. The glob search for `**/custom_nodes/**` returned no results. This directory would need to be created as part of the task described in `task_config.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. References to `UnitStats`, `BattleUnit`, and `Team` Enum\n\n### `UnitStats` references (10 occurrences):\n\n| File | Line(s) | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd` | 1 | `class_name UnitStats` definition |\n| `/workspace/data/units/bjorn.tres` | 1 | `script_class=\"UnitStats\"` |\n| `/workspace/data/enemies/zombie.tres` | 1 | `script_class=\"UnitStats\"` |\n| `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` | 4, 12 | `@export var stats: UnitStats` and `func _set_stats(value: UnitStats)` |\n| `/workspace/task_config.json` | 2 | Referenced in the task instruction |\n| `/workspace/.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10` | 6, 8, 9 | Cache entries for tres and gd files |\n| `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg` | 11 | Registered script class `UnitStats` with base `Resource` |\n\n### `BattleUnit` references (5 occurrences):\n\n| File | Line(s) | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` | 1 | `class_name BattleUnit` definition |\n| `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn` | 9 | `[node name=\"BattleUnit\" type=\"Area2D\"]` |\n| `/workspace/task_config.json` | 2 | Referenced in the task instruction |\n| `/workspace/.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10` | 13 | Cache entry for the script |\n| `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg` | 3 | Registered script class `BattleUnit` with base `Area2D` |\n\n### `Team` enum references:\n\nThe `Team` enum is defined in `/workspace/data/units/unit_stats.gd` at line 4:\n```gdscript\nenum Team {PLAYER, ENEMY}\n```\n\nIt is used implicitly via `stats.team` in:\n- `/workspace/scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` line 19: `collision_layer = stats.team + 1`\n- `/workspace/data/units/bjorn.tres` line 7: `team = 0` (PLAYER)\n- `/workspace/data/enemies/zombie.tres` line 7: `team = 1` (ENEMY)\n\nThe grep for `Team\\s*(enum|class)` found no separate `Team` enum/class definition beyond the one inside `unit_stats.gd` (the regex requiring `enum` or `class` right after `Team` did not match because of the extra spaces/newline in the actual source).\n\n---\n\n## Supporting Files\n\n### `/workspace/task_config.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Implement the hero-versus-goblin aggro targeting setup from the tutorial. In `res://data/units/unit_stats.gd`, define `TARGET = { Team.PLAYER: \\\"goblins\\\", Team.ENEMY: \\\"heroes\\\" }` so units can look up the opposing group name from their team. Create `res://custom_nodes/detect_range.gd` as `class_name DetectRange` extending `Area2D` with exported `col_shape: CollisionShape2D`, `base_range_size: float`, and `stats: UnitStats`; when `stats` is assigned, set `collision_layer` to `4 * (stats.team + 1)`, set `collision_mask` to `2 - stats.team`, and replace the collision shape with a `CircleShape2D` whose radius is `base_range_size * stats.attack_range`. Create `res://custom_nodes/target_finder.gd` as `class_name TargetFinder` extending `Node` with an exported `actor: BattleUnit`, a `target: BattleUnit`, a `targets_in_range: Array[BattleUnit]`, and a `targets_in_range_changed` signal. On ready, connect the actor's `DetectRange.area_entered` and `area_exited` signals to handlers that append or erase only `BattleUnit` instances and emit `targets_in_range_changed`. Implement `find_target()` so it uses `UnitStats.TARGET`, `get_nodes_in_group()`, and `distance_squared_to()` to store the closest opposing `BattleUnit` in `target`, and implement `has_target_in_range()` to return whether `targets_in_range` is non-empty. In `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn`, add a `DetectRange` Area2D child with a `CollisionShape2D` child and a sibling `TargetFinder` node, wire both to the battle unit, and in `res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.gd` expose them as `detect_range` and `target_finder` onready variables while assigning `detect_range.stats = stats` when battle-unit stats are set.\"\n}\n```\n\n### `/workspace/data/units/bjorn.tres`:\n```gdresource\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 0\nattack_range = 3\n```\n\n### `/workspace/data/enemies/zombie.tres`:\n```gdresource\n[gd_resource type=\"Resource\" script_class=\"UnitStats\" load_steps=2 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"Script\" path=\"res://data/units/unit_stats.gd\" id=\"1_unit_stats\"]\n\n[resource]\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_unit_stats\")\nteam = 1\nattack_range = 1\n```\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`:\n```gdresource\n[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://scenes/battle_unit/battle_unit.tscn\" id=\"1_battle_unit\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/units/bjorn.tres\" id=\"2_player_stats\"]\n[ext_resource type=\"Resource\" path=\"res://data/enemies/zombie.tres\" id=\"3_enemy_stats\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node2D\"]\n\n[node name=\"HeroUnit\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"heroes\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(0, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"2_player_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"GoblinNear\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"goblins\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(70, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"3_enemy_stats\")\n\n[node name=\"GoblinFar\" parent=\".\" groups=[\"goblins\"] instance=ExtResource(\"1_battle_unit\")]\nposition = Vector2(140, 0)\nstats = ExtResource(\"3_enemy_stats\")\n```\n\nThis main scene instantiates three `BattleUnit` instances: one hero (group \"heroes\", using `bjorn.tres` with team=PLAYER, attack_range=3) and two goblins (group \"goblins\", using `zombie.tres` with team=ENEMY, attack_range=1). They are placed horizontally at x=0, 70, and 140.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f21adfe5bffenhUxDN7qtJawe5","sessionId":"ses_f21ada94effeuR5QrQhVWvHA7m","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790436333237,"end":1790436439746}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_591d1df0-2fe9-4371-819d-ad0629fc9777"}},"id":"prt_0de5256aa001DrV8o3yE6iOpXI","sessionID":"ses_f21adfe5bffenhUxDN7qtJawe5","messageID":"msg_0de52037f001AKDAICXjvVZ6gY"}}
